Subject: [PATCH v3 0/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's mail hub
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:40:27 +0000

This builds the hub that "[PATCH v2] jails/instances/lab-mail: Spec
the list's mail hub" [1] describes, on b/dev. It turns the relay jail
into the list's home in steps, one service at a time. Each step
leaves a jail that works and does what its README.org says.

- Patch 1 corrects the spec on what Dovecot does to a reader's write.
  A STORE or EXPUNGE answers OK and changes nothing; only append,
  copy, and move are refused. Acceptance step 7 now expects that.
- Patch 2 makes Dovecot the only writer of the list. mbsync still
  fetches one way, but into Dovecot over IMAP as the login mbsync,
  not into the maildir. Readers see no change. This is the one step
  that needs the maildir and mbsync's state emptied first.
- Patch 3 turns the fetch into a two-way sync of lists and Archive.
- Patch 4 adds Pat's login, so he can archive and delete on lab-mail.
- Patch 5 swaps smtprelay for OpenSMTPD, which hands posts to Dovecot
  over LMTP. smtprelay, jq, and the mailcred group go with it. Posts
  land in INBOX, since LMTP alone delivers only there.
- Patch 6 adds check-message, which refuses a malformed post.
- Patch 7 documents the one-time import of the jj maildir.
- Patch 8 is the proposal from v2, unchanged: a Sieve script from
  Pigeonhole files each post into lists, as the spec says.

The tree after patch 7 is identical to v2's after its patch 2, and
the tree after patch 8 is identical to v1's and v2's. The tests in
the v2 cover letter [2] therefore still hold for the end of the
series. For the steps between, I checked that every script passes
sh -n (check-message, awk), and that dist.mtree lists exactly the
files under dist/ at every step. Dovecot, smtpd, and the jail build
are not installed here, so no intermediate step was run.

Changes in v3:
- The old patch 2, "Carry the list instead of relaying it", is split
  into patches 2 to 7, one logical change each, so the series grows
  the hub instead of replacing it in one commit (Pat). Patch 2 opens
  the README's rights section, and each later step extends it.
